@@ -173,6 +173,31 @@ configuring the GLib library:
 : This option requires DTrace support. If it is available, then GLib will also
   check for the presence of SystemTap.
 
+`-Dopenssl=false` and `-Dopenssl=true`
+: Enable or disable the OpenSSL-backed `GHmac` implementation.
+  The OpenSSL backend is Linux-only, requires OpenSSL 3.x APIs at build time,
+  and dynamically loads `libcrypto.so.3` at runtime. There is no fallback to
+  another backend if loading or symbol resolution fails. `-Dopenssl=true`
+  cannot be combined with `-Dgnutls=true`. The key length accepted by
+  `g_hmac_new()` is limited to `G_MAXINT` with this backend.
+
+  Backend initialization and digest/key acceptance are governed by the
+  application's active OpenSSL provider and property configuration. A failed
+  provider fetch or policy rejection causes GHmac construction to return `%NULL`.
+  This backend does not force providers, set default properties, or claim FIPS
+  certification.
+
+  This backend keeps GLib itself free of direct `libcrypto` link requirements:
+  static GLib consumers still need a shared `libcrypto.so.3` and provider data
+  at runtime. It is not a hermetic fully static crypto deployment.
+
+  Thread-safety rules are unchanged: reference counting and independent GHmac
+  instances are safe; callers must synchronize concurrent mutation or reads of a
+  single instance.
+
+  GLib does not own the process-wide OpenSSL lifecycle. Applications must avoid
+  using or unreffing GHmac objects after OpenSSL cleanup/teardown.
+
 `-Db_coverage=true` and `-Db_coverage=false`
