From c759974b1ebd45bcf8aecfadc93630605fc09bdd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tobias Brick <tobiasb@microsoft.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 05:07:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 8/9] docs(glib): explain openssl loader failure recovery

Document process-lifetime loader and required-symbol failure caching,
one-time warning and restart after runtime repair. Distinguish recoverable
provider and property-policy rejection from cached loader failure.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Copilot-Session: ebcf9f4b-5364-45c7-a0a7-6f274f5971c2
---
 docs/reference/glib/building.md | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/docs/reference/glib/building.md b/docs/reference/glib/building.md
index 0eba171a87e988c6f153461c37dcf77dd0a03ec1..0eae6f2362773d48f61523482b6c6fb5a39052c1 100644
--- a/docs/reference/glib/building.md
+++ b/docs/reference/glib/building.md
@@ -181,12 +181,21 @@ configuring the GLib library:
   cannot be combined with `-Dgnutls=true`. The key length accepted by
   `g_hmac_new()` is limited to `G_MAXINT` with this backend.
 
+  Loading or required-symbol resolution failures are cached for the lifetime
+  of the process. Only the first failure emits a warning; subsequent GHmac
+  constructions return `%NULL` without retrying. After repairing the runtime
+  installation, restart the process.
+
   Backend initialization and digest/key acceptance are governed by the
   application's active OpenSSL provider and property configuration. A failed
   provider fetch or policy rejection causes GHmac construction to return `%NULL`.
   This backend does not force providers, set default properties, or claim FIPS
   certification.
 
+  Unlike loader failures, provider or property-policy rejection does not
+  permanently disable subsequent GHmac construction. Later constructions can
+  succeed if the application's provider and property configuration permits it.
+
   This backend keeps GLib itself free of direct `libcrypto` link requirements:
   static GLib consumers still need a shared `libcrypto.so.3` and provider data
   at runtime. It is not a hermetic fully static crypto deployment.
From 9653c9da8e39ae799655be17b89774786637ba1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tobias Brick <tobiasb@microsoft.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 05:07:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] build(glib): reject mismatched openssl function
 declarations

Make incompatible-pointer diagnostics fatal only in the OpenSSL signature
probe. Require compiler support explicitly rather than silently weakening
the ABI check; leave project-wide warning policy unchanged.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Copilot-Session: ebcf9f4b-5364-45c7-a0a7-6f274f5971c2
---
 meson.build | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
index ed0bd3d427b5fb1d0ca2ef2ebf64b5dd477bd2fc..172f2caea746ceafddf9743e098828216aa26041 100644
--- a/meson.build
+++ b/meson.build
@@ -2396,6 +2396,11 @@ elif get_option('openssl')
     static : false,
     allow_fallback : false)
 
+  openssl_type_check_arg = '-Werror=incompatible-pointer-types'
+  if not cc.has_argument(openssl_type_check_arg)
+    error('OpenSSL GHmac backend requires compiler support for ' + openssl_type_check_arg)
+  endif
+
   openssl_decl_check = '''
     #include <openssl/core_names.h>
     #include <openssl/err.h>
@@ -2456,7 +2461,10 @@ elif get_option('openssl')
       (void) clear_f;
       return 0;
     }'''
-  if not cc.compiles(openssl_decl_check, dependencies : libcrypto_dep, name : 'OpenSSL GHmac declarations')
+  if not cc.compiles(openssl_decl_check,
+      dependencies : libcrypto_dep,
+      args : openssl_type_check_arg,
+      name : 'OpenSSL GHmac declarations')
     error('OpenSSL GHmac backend requires OpenSSL 3 EVP_MAC and ERR mark declarations')
   endif
 
